/datum/lore/character_background/origin/species/scori/ondosida
	name = "Ondo-Sida"
	id = "origin_scori_ondosida"
	category = "Surt"
	innate_languages = list(LANGUAGE_ID_SIGN)
	desc = "A tribe of scorians located most closely to where Nanotrasen originally set up exploratory mining operations on the planet Surt. \
    As a consequence, when the scorians were first driven from the depths by the shifting tectonic cycles of the planet, they were the first \
	to make contact. As word of the outlanders spread further they were eventually given the task of dealing with them by their overlords the \
	Itema-Arishrim, a role that has proven controversial to the tribe over the years even as relations slowly improved. These scorians are the \
	most likely among settled scorians to tolerate contact with outsiders, and their contact with the outside universe has started to have some \
	effects on their particular culture. The name 'Ondo-Sida' translates roughly to 'Stone Boundary,' poetically referring to the sharply \
	contrasting geological strata of the tribe's original home. It has taken on a more metaphorical meaning now as the first contact most \
	outlanders will have with any elements of scorian culture."

/datum/lore/character_background/origin/species/scori/atdarimdaar
    name = "Atdarim-Daar"
    id = "origin_scori_atdarimdaar"
    category = "Surt"
    desc = "Translating as 'Embers of Truth' the Atdarim-Daar are a tribe of scorians insular even by the usual standards of the species' culture. \
    They believe that fire can burn away impurities in oneself, often engaging in ritualistic branding and scarification to signify one's station or \
	even acceptance among the tribe. Wandering scorians find little assistance when entering their lands, unless they stay and spend a prolonged \
	period proving their worth and dedication. Subjects of the Itema-Arishrim alongside the Ondo-Sida, a generational grudge exists between the elders of both tribes, \
	the Atdarim-Daar blaming the Ondo-Sida for their subjugation. Scorians belonging to this tribe often need to travel through Ondo-Sidan lands in order to hunt, \
	forage, or simply to transport taxes and tribute demanded by the empire."

/datum/lore/character_background/origin/species/scori/wanderer
    name = "Wanderer"
    id = "origin_scori_wanderer"
    category = "Surt"
    innate_languages = list(LANGUAGE_ID_SIGN)
    desc = "Some scorians choose to leave their original tribes or homes, electing instead to wander the wastes both above and below the surface of Surt. \
    These scorians are the most difficult to pin down to any one cultural basis, though they often take on the role of trader or mercenary, some even chosing \
    to deal with the sky people."
